    "updated_at": "2022-02-20T04:39:56Z",
    "body": "> Do you resolve links? If not, that might be the problem.\r\n\r\nI just tried to reproduce this error with a symlink to the editor, and it worked fine on `1.3.0` on `linux`, so I don't believe links are a problem.\r\n\r\n```\r\n~/bin\r\n❯ \\ls -l $(which $EDITOR) $(which $VISUAL)\r\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 j users 13 Feb 19 19:27 /home/j/bin/pico -> /usr/bin/nano\r\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 j users 13 Feb 19 19:27 /home/j/bin/pico -> /usr/bin/nano\r\n\r\n~/bin\r\n❯ starship config  # worked fine\r\n\r\n~/bin\r\n❯ rm pico\r\n\r\n~/bin\r\n❯ starship config\r\nthread 'main' panicked at 'Unable to locate editor in $PATH.: Custom { kind: NotFound, error: CannotFindBinaryPath }', src/configure.rs:274:10\r\nnote: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace\r\n```\r\n\r\n@jwezel Could you please provide the output of:\r\n```\r\necho EDITOR=\"$EDITOR\"\r\nwhich \"$EDITOR\" &&\r\nrealpath -e \"$(which \"$EDITOR\")\" &&\r\nls -l \"$(realpath -e \"$(which \"$EDITOR\")\")\"\r\necho VISUAL=\"$VISUAL\"\r\nwhich \"$VISUAL\" &&\r\nrealpath -e \"$(which \"$VISUAL\")\" &&\r\nls -l \"$(realpath -e \"$(which \"$VISUAL\")\")\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso, I notice you reported against `0.53.0`, is this error still present if upgraded to `1.3.0`?",
